 {
  "index": 7,
  "label": "text",
  "content": "The first mile leaves the town by the river and turns, quite suddenly, into reeds. Nobody had told us how quickly Colchester ends. By ten in the morning the only sound was the wind in the saltmarsh grass and a curlew complaining somewhere to our left.",
