 {
  "index": 10,
  "label": "text",
  "content": "Aisha Pritchard, who keeps the oyster shed at the island's end, says the crossing has not changed in her lifetime, only the people on it. Her grandmother, she told us, walked it in clogs. We followed her advice and kept to the posts, and reached the far shore with wet boots and a good appetite.",
  "bbox_2d": [
   31,
   749,
   628,
   847
  ],
